mother's day is sunday and if you  haven't gotten you something for mom yet  you better do it soon because you know  we're running out of time flowers of  course are always a really popular  option but a late purchase could leave  you empty-handed jeremy ford tells us  how inflation is certainly affecting our  local floral industry  with mother's day on the horizon some  floral companies are facing post  pandemic challenges in preparation for  sunday i have been in this industry all  my life i have never seen inflation  affect flowers the way the pandemic has  caused this along with everything else  we've seen in the past couple of years  michelle joy howard is the founder of  floor couture she says during the  pandemic a lot of farms closed putting a  damper on product availability  they were bought out by big  conglomerates that only do flowers and  chains like your big box stores the  change that we've just seen is drastic  we're talking anywhere from 20 to 40  percent difference in the price of  flowers  next door howard's sister deborah newson  bavina is the owner of las vegas floral  and plant wholesale she tells me  inflation is hurting the industry and  driving prices out of control gas prices  are affecting the price of flowers the  cost of labor the cost of fertilizer yet  she refuses to let it stop her from  fulfilling orders and getting your  flowers in the hands of loved ones  overall we've been able to fulfill  95 percent of our orders there have been  a few shortages but  thank goodness our clientele has been  amazing because a single flower can have  a big impact on an emotional heart  whether it's self-care or you're trying  to give your emotions to somebody else  we love it and we love to make life blue  jeremy j ford live local now
 

